From: Ralf Erlebach <ralf@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the behaviour type archetypal

question_behaviour_type::is_archetypal() returns false by default, and
qbehaviour_stackmathgame_type does not override it. That has two consequences,
neither of which points at the cause:

  1. question_engine::get_archetypal_behaviours() builds the list offered in the
     quiz "Question behaviour" menu. A non-archetypal behaviour is left out, so a
     teacher cannot select STACK Math Game for a quiz at all.

  2. If the value reaches quiz.preferredbehaviour by any other route - a
     generator, a restore, an SQL update - then
     question_engine::make_archetypal_behaviour() throws
     "The requested behaviour is not actually an archetypal one" the moment a
     student starts an attempt.

Symptom 2 is what local_stackmathgame's Behat run hit: four scenarios failed on
"I press Attempt quiz" with a coding exception, several layers away from the
missing method.

An archetypal behaviour is simply one a quiz may be set to, which is exactly what
this behaviour is for.

--- a/behaviourtype.php
+++ b/behaviourtype.php
@@ -11,6 +11,17 @@
  */
 class qbehaviour_stackmathgame_type extends question_behaviour_type {
     /**
+     * This behaviour is meant to be chosen as a quiz's preferred behaviour.
+     *
+     * Without this, Moodle omits it from the quiz question behaviour menu and
+     * question_engine::make_archetypal_behaviour() refuses to instantiate it.
+     *
+     * @return bool
+     */
+    public function is_archetypal() {
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    /**
      * Questions can finish during the attempt, matching adaptive STACK flows.
      *
      * @return bool
